<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26014" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Latmus</span></b> , i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λάτμος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mountain in Caria, at the mouth of the
				Mæander, where Luna (Selene) kissed the sleeping
				Endymion</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc. 1, 38, 92</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 1,
			17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 29, 31, §
			113</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Latmĭus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Mount Latmus, Latmian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Latmius Endymion,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. A.
					A. 3, 84</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venator,</span>”
				<i>Endymion</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 8, 28</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Latmĭădēus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., the same; of <i>Endymion</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 9, §
			919</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
